      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-145619",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Let the joint CDF of $X$ and $Y$ be $F(x, y)$, where\n\n$F(10, 9) = 0.72, F(10, 6) = 0.3, F(8, 9) = 0.15, F(8, 6) = 0.08$,\n\nand the supports of $X$ and $Y$, respectively, are\n\n$S_{X} = {2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12}, S_{Y} = {3, 6, 9, 12}$.\n\nFind $P(8 < X \\le 10, 6 < Y \\le 9)$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
